# Citation metadata (https://citation-file-format.github.io/). GitHub shows it
# as "Cite this repository". Keep version in step with pyproject.toml
# (tests/test_packaging.py checks it).
# TODO(owner): replace the "FiberHMM Authors" entity with the individual
# authors (family-names, given-names, orcid), and add date-released and a DOI
# once the release is tagged and archived; add a preferred-citation for the
# publication when it is available (docs/about/citing.md says the same).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FiberHMM in published work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "FiberHMM: chromatin footprint calling from single-molecule Fiber-seq and DAF-seq data"
version: 3.0.0
authors:
  - name: "FiberHMM Authors"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/fiberseq/FiberHMM"
url: "https://fiberseq.github.io/FiberHMM/"
abstract: >-
  FiberHMM calls chromatin footprints on single DNA molecules from the
  modification marks of Fiber-seq (m6A) and DAF-seq (deamination) reads,
  writes them back into the BAM as standard tags, and finds recurrent
  footprint classes across molecules at a locus.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - chromatin
  - fiber-seq
  - DAF-seq
  - hidden-markov-model
  - nucleosome
  - footprinting
  - single-molecule
